     Monitor the disk usage of the minion
@@ -83,6 +105,31 @@ def beacon(config):
     which means that if a regular expression matches another defined mount point,
     it will override the previously defined threshold.
 
+    A mount can also be configured with a ``min`` and/or ``max`` threshold
+    instead of a bare percentage. ``max`` behaves exactly like the plain
+    percentage form above (alert when usage rises to or above the
+    threshold), while ``min`` alerts when usage drops to or below the
+    threshold. This is useful for catching a mount that normally runs busy
+    but suddenly reports near-empty, which usually means the filesystem
+    failed to mount rather than that space was actually freed.
+
+    .. code-block:: yaml
+
+        beacons:
+          diskusage:
+            - /mnt/nfs:
+                min: 10%
+                max: 90%
+
+    ``min`` and ``max`` can also be used independently:
+
+    .. code-block:: yaml
+
+        beacons:
+          diskusage:
+            - /mnt/nfs:
+                min: 10%
+
